---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import InputDemo from '../../components/InputDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Input" description="A single-line text field for names, emails, numbers, dates, and searches.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Input</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A single-line text field. Use it for names, emails, tokens, numbers, dates, times, and inline searches.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <InputDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Input usage"
      code={`import { Field } from "@base-ui/react/field";
import { Input } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/input";

const [name, setName] = useState("");

<Field.Root invalid={!name.trim()}>
  <Field.Label>Agent name</Field.Label>
  <Input
    value={name}
    maxLength={120}
    placeholder="People Ops helper"
    onChange={(event) => setName(event.target.value)}
  />
  <Field.Error match>Enter a name.</Field.Error>
</Field.Root>

<label htmlFor="site">Site ID</label>
<Input id="site" aria-describedby="site-help" />

<Input scale="lg" type="email" placeholder="you@company.com" autoComplete="email" />`}
    />
    <p>
      Input renders a native <code>input</code> and takes every input prop:
      <code>value</code> or <code>defaultValue</code>, <code>onChange</code>
      (or Base UI's <code>onValueChange</code>), <code>ref</code>,<code>required</code>, <code>maxLength</code>,{' '}
      <code>pattern</code>,<code>autoComplete</code>, <code>inputMode</code>, and event handlers such as{' '}
      <code>onKeyDown</code> and <code>onPaste</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>scale</code> is <code>"default"</code> (32px tall, 10px side padding, 14px text) or <code>"lg"</code> (44px,
      12px padding, 16px text). Use <code>lg</code> for sign-in and onboarding forms.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>type</code> can be any native type. Cloud uses text, email, password, number, url, date, time,
      datetime-local, and file. A visible file input styles its button to match. A hidden file input (
      <code>hidden</code>, <code>tabIndex={'{-1}'}</code>,<code>aria-hidden</code>) can be opened with{' '}
      <code>ref.current.click()</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>disabled</code> dims the input and blocks edits.
      <code>readOnly</code> keeps it focusable and selectable, which suits copy fields and saving states.{' '}
      <code>aria-invalid</code> draws a danger border and focus ring. The input sets <code>data-slot="input"</code> and
      <code>data-scale</code>; you can pass your own <code>data-slot</code> and
      <code>className</code> to set it inside another control.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">With a field</h2>
    <p>
      Input is a Base UI <code>Input</code>, so it works inside Base UI
      <code>Field.Root</code>. The field gives it an id, labels it with
      <code>Field.Label</code>, describes it with <code>Field.Description</code>
      and <code>Field.Error</code>, and passes <code>disabled</code> and
      <code>invalid</code>. Without a field, pair <code>id</code> with a label's <code>htmlFor</code>, or use{' '}
      <code>aria-label</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">SidebarInput</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Sidebar search"
      code={`import { SidebarHeader, SidebarInput } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/sidebar";

<SidebarHeader>
  <SidebarInput aria-label="Search sample sidebar" placeholder="Search locally…" />
</SidebarHeader>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>SidebarInput</code> is a default-scale Input on the canvas color, with
      <code>data-slot="sidebar-input"</code> and
      <code>data-sidebar="input"</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Every input needs a name: a field label, a label with
      <code>htmlFor</code>, or <code>aria-label</code>. Point
      <code>aria-describedby</code> at help and error text. A focused input shows a 2px focus ring, red when invalid.
      Read-only inputs stay in the tab order; disabled ones leave it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Color changes take 120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested. In forced colors mode the input keeps a system
      border and a highlight focus ring.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The border uses <code>--sprout-input</code>, the fill
      <code>--sprout-surface</code>, text <code>--sprout-text</code>, and the placeholder <code>--sprout-muted</code>.
      Focus uses
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>, invalid <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and disabled <code>--sprout-hover</code>.
      Radius follows
      <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>. The opt-in TulipFarm theme tints the focus ring through these tokens.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
